{
	title: 'Context graph: context size per block on a web page',
	spec: "The status row context number (terminal: one OSC 8 link around the whole number group, hidden target from ansi.webUrl so it carries the link code; web: an <a href> around the group, keeping its heat colours; touch target 44px on coarse pointers) opens /context/<session> under the host webUrl, an authenticated read-only no-store page (same login gate and one-time code as the changes pages; unknown session 404; src/host/context-page.ts, routed in web.fetch beside the file pages). It plots the session context size over its history as plain SVG built on the host from history (no chart library): one stacked bar per provider round, x = round with turn boundaries marked (dotted line, t<turn> labels) and the date on hover (SVG title), y = the round input tokens split into cache read, cache write and uncached input (status-cool/warm/hot colours from the host theme, none written in the page), the model context window as a dashed line (per point, following /model changes; named in the key). Data: every provider round with usage appends a history record { type: round, usage, model?, block? } after its assistant blocks (block = record number of the round first block, the link target /<session>#<block>); it is not provider input and not shown in the transcript. Turns from before round records show as one approximate point from their turn_end context. Drops are labelled only where history knows the cause: compaction or clear (a compact/reset record between two rounds), pruning checkpoint (the completed-turn count since the last boundary crossed a multiple of pruning.batchTurns() and the total fell more than 10%), cache miss (cache read fell under 10% of the previous round with over 1000 read, while the total did not fall); other drops stay unlabelled. Each cause is a coloured dashed line with a letter (C, X, P, M), listed below the chart (newest 50) with links to the block. Tapping a bar shows its round, tokens and a link to the block in a line under the chart (a bar is an <a href> to the block, so without script it just navigates); hover shows the same in a title. Wider than the screen, the bars scroll sideways inside the chart frame only (the y axis stays put, the newest round is scrolled into view), the page keeps its one scroller and no overflow. Live: /context/<session>/events is a text/event-stream (server timeout off for it) that receives the whole redrawn graph markup whenever stats.round or stats.ended runs (a finished provider round or turn end), which the page swaps in keeping its scroll; the browser never polls. The page script is one nonce-CSP inline script (no other scripts, connect-src self). Retro look per tasks/README.md: square corners, cyan border, no glow. A page or stream for a closed session never opens it (its model is read from its metadata without keeping it open), and the existence check reads no other session's metadata. /auth revoke ends every open event stream, as it closes every socket.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Per-round usage was not in history (only the turn_end sum and last context), so this task adds the round record (history.record writes it after flush; replay.toMessages, transcript.recordShown and history.recordTypes ignore or list it). Existing tests that listed a turn records now include it. Old histories degrade to one approximate point per turn from turn_end.context.',
		'Pruning checkpoints are not recorded anywhere (pruning.ts keeps only projection.ason), so the graph derives them the same way pruning does: completed turn_end count since the last compact/reset, per batchTurns. A pressure rewrite (0d) is therefore not labelled; its drop stays unlabelled. Making pruning write a history/diag mark would let it be named.',
		'Live push hooks stats.round/stats.ended (not host.broadcast: host.ts sits at the 400-line limit). The status-row link text and the c4 page were checked in headless Chrome at 1200 and 390 px wide (coarse pointer via setTouchEmulationEnabled; setEmulatedMedia for pointer does not apply): no page overflow, y axis fixed while bars scroll, bar tap fills the info line, a round appended after load appears without reload, status link is 44px tall on touch.',
		"Considered and declined (30 Sep): reading a closed session's history in slices on page load. Decoding is about 4 ms/MB and histories are usually under 1 MB, so the one synchronous read costs a few ms; chunked async reading was not worth its code."
	],
	needs: ['k5', 'e3', '0d']
}
